    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n47975" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">testĭcŭlus</span></b> , i,
			m.
		dim.
		2. testis, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>a testicle.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>, <i><span class="en">Auct. Her. 3,
				20, 33</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Juv. 6, 339</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Mart. 3,
				24, 5</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Cels. 7,
			18</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>, as a designation of <i>manly vigor</i>, <i>manliness</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">haec fierent, si testiculi vena ulla paterni
					Viveret in nobis?</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Pers.
					1, 103</span></i>
			.— </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>III.</b>
			<i>The name of a plant</i>,
				<i><span class="en">App. Herb. 15</span></i>.</div>
